     {"id":47219,"name":"Apis mellifera","preferred_common_name":"Western Honey Bee","wikipedia_summary":"The <b>western honey bee</b> or <b>European honey bee</b> (<i>Apis mellifera</i>) is the most common of the 7–12 species of honey bee worldwide. The genus name <i>Apis</i> is Latin for \"bee\", and <i>mellifera</i> is the Latin for \"honey-bearing\", referring to the species' production of honey for the winter.","ancestor_ids":[48460,1,47120,372739,47158,184884,47201,124417,326777,47222,630955,47221,199939,538904,47220,578086]},
     {"id":53720,"name":"Melia azedarach","preferred_common_name":"Chinaberry","wikipedia_summary":"<i><b>Melia azedarach</b></i>, commonly known by many names, including <b>chinaberry tree</b>, <b>Pride of India</b>, <b>bead-tree</b>, <b>Cape lilac</b>, <b>syringa berrytree</b>, <b>Persian lilac</b>, and <b>Indian lilac</b>, is a species of deciduous tree in the mahogany family, Meliaceae, that is native to Indomalaya and Australasia.","ancestor_ids":[48460,47126,211194,47125,47124,47729,53724,1510860,1510861,53725]},
     {"id":84364,"name":"Chasmanthium latifolium","preferred_common_name":"river oats","wikipedia_summary":"<i><b>Chasmanthium latifolium</b></i>, known as <b>woodoats</b>, <b>inland sea oats</b>, <b>northern sea oats</b>, and <b>river oats</b> is a grass native to the central and eastern United States, Manitoba, and northeastern Mexico; it grows as far north as Pennsylvania and Michigan, where it is a threatened species. The species was previously classified as <i>Uniola latifolia</i> (André Michaux).","ancestor_ids":[48460,47126,211194,47125,47163,47162,47434,326013,956879,84365]},
     {"id":119960,"name":"Berchemia scandens","preferred_common_name":"Supplejack","wikipedia_summary":"<i><b>Berchemia scandens</b></i>, the <b>Rattan vine</b> or <b>Alabama supplejack</b>, is a species of climbing plant in the buckthorn family Rhamnaceae. It is native to the central and southern parts of the United States.","ancestor_ids":[48460,47126,211194,47125,47124,47132,49041,1256740,119962]},
     {"id":126424,"name":"Parthenium hysterophorus","preferred_common_name":"Santa Maria feverfew","wikipedia_summary":"<i><b>Parthenium hysterophorus</b></i> is a species of flowering plant in the aster family, Asteraceae. It is native to the American tropics. Common names include <b>Santa-Maria</b>, <b>Santa Maria feverfew</b>, <b>whitetop weed</b>, <b>famine weed</b>, and <b>congress weed</b>. In India, it is locally known as <b>carrot grass, congress grass</b> or <i><b>Gajar Ghans</b></i>. It is a common invasive species in India, Australia, and parts of Africa.","ancestor_ids":[48460,47126,211194,47125,47124,47605,47604,632790,605446,639449,83894]},
     {"id":153490,"name":"Paronychia virginica","preferred_common_name":"Whitlow-wort","wikipedia_summary":null,"ancestor_ids":[48460,47126,211194,47125,47124,47366,48567,791430,71144]},
     {"id":204420,"name":"Strophostyles helvola","preferred_common_name":"trailing fuzzy-bean","wikipedia_summary":"<i><b>Strophostyles helvola</b></i> (sometimes spelled <i>S. helvula</i>) is a species of flowering plant in the legume family known by the common names <b>amberique-bean</b>, <b>trailing wild bean</b>, and <b>trailing fuzzy-bean</b>. It is native to eastern Canada and the eastern United States.","ancestor_ids":[48460,47126,211194,47125,47124,47123,47122,507502,507503,533399,130996]},
